{
  "workflowId": "100002355226949",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_FIN_AP_PAYMENT_PROCESS_REQUEST_TEMPLATE_ANALYST",
  "name": "Payment Process Request Template Analyst",
  "description": "Assists payables specialists in retrieving specific payment request template data. This analyst identifies details using criteria such as template names or dynamic discounting filters. While it facilitates information discovery, it does not modify existing templates or create new payment process request templates.",
  "specification": {
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768144219728"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Identify Query type"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768144678648"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_IDENTIFY_QUERY_TYPE",
          "id": "1768144219728",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768144219730_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use your intelligence to identify the filter from {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \nChat history: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory }}\n\nIdentify which kind of following query user is asking:\n\n1. Get PPR templates by Business Unit and Currency\nUse this when the user asks for PPR templates by a business unit and currency, or when the query mentions a business unit and a currency together, even if the user also mentions:\n- payment programs\n- supported payment programs\n- supply chain financing\n- virtual card program\n- dynamic discounting\n→ Output: getPprTemplateByBUandCurrency\n\n2. Fuzzy match PPR templates based on a name the user gives\n\nUser mentions: template with name like\n→ Output: getPprTemplateByName\n\n3. Get PPR templates related to Dynamic Discount (DD) or early payment criteria\n\nUser mentions: Dynamic Discount, DD, early payment, termination date (this includes positive matches, exclusions, or complex conditions like \"don't include\" or \"don't only include\")\n→ Output: getPprTemplateForDD\n\n4. Get PPR template by other filters\n\nUser mentions other status that cannot be categorized as one of the above\n→ Output: others\n\nExample:\n- Is there any template has similar name to CPPOT_020042?\n  Output: getPprTemplateByName\n- Are there any template that has MNO in it?\n  Output: getPprTemplateByName\n- Tell me the PPR templates that can select early payment invoices.\n  Output: getPprTemplateForDD\n- Templates that don't only include DD invoices\n  Output: getPprTemplateForDD\n- Templates that don't include DD invoices\n  Output: getPprTemplateForDD\n- Show PPR templates for supplier Vision Operations\n  Output: others\n- Show PPR templates that use Brazil Check payment method\n  Output: others\n- Show all templates and classify them by DD behavior.\n  Output: others\n- Show payment process request templates for Virtual credit card program in Vision Operations for USD\n   Output : getPprTemplateByBUandCurrency\n-Show payment process request templates for supported Payment Programs in Vision Operations for USD\n  Output : getPprTemplateByBUandCurrency\n\n#Guard rail\n- Don’t add any other information other than the four keywords mentioned above\n\n# DD-coded template name rule:\t\nIf the user explicitly asks for a template by name, named, with name, exact name, or details for a specific template value such as PPR_ExcludeDD, PPR_IncludeDDOnly, or PPR_TestOne, classify the query as getPprTemplateByName.\t\nDo not treat DD inside a specific template name as a Dynamic Discount criteria search.\t\nOnly classify as getPprTemplateForDD when the user asks for DD / Dynamic Discount / early payment templates as a category or capability.\t\nExamples:\t\n- \"Are there any ppr template with name PPR_ExcludeDD?\" -> getPprTemplateByName\t\n- \"Is there any template named PPR_IncludeDDOnly?\" -> getPprTemplateByName\t\n- \"Show templates containing DD\" -> getPprTemplateForDD\t\n- \"Show DD templates\" -> getPprTemplateForDD"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query Router"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "getPprTemplateForDD": "1768144709479",
            "others": "1769704630143",
            "getPprTemplateByName": "1768144790816",
            "getPprTemplateByBUandCurrency": "1780570364269"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_QUERY_ROUTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1768144678648",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768144678649_1",
